        <li><a href="#guest-demand">Guest Demand &amp; Review Activity</a></li>
        <li><a href="#availability">Availability &amp; Booking Constraints</a></li>
        <li><a href="#key-takeaways">Key Takeaways &amp; Strategic Implications</a></li>
    </ol>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 1 -->
<div class="section" id="market-overview">
    <h2><span class="section-num">1</span>Global Market Overview</h2>
    <p class="section-objective">Summarize the total number of listings per city, overall price distribution, and room-type breakdown to establish the scale and composition of each market.</p>
    <div class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-value">50,000</div><div class="kpi-label">Total Listings</div></div>
        <div class="kpi-card alt"><div class="kpi-value">7</div><div class="kpi-label">Cities Covered</div></div>
        <div class="kpi-card accent"><div class="kpi-value">4</div><div class="kpi-label">Room Types</div></div>
        <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-value">48.1%</div><div class="kpi-label">Price Data Coverage</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-container"><canvas id="chartListingsPerCity"></canvas></div>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>City</th><th>Total Listings</th><th>Entire Home/Apt</th><th>Private Room</th><th>Shared Room</th><th>Hotel Room</th><th>Listings w/ Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>""" + render_rows(table_overview_rows) + """</tbody>
    </table></div>
    <div class="chart-container"><canvas id="chartRoomTypeMix"></canvas></div>
    <div class="highlight-box"><strong>Key Observation:</strong> London and Paris together account for """ + str(int(london_paris_share)) + """% of all listings, reflecting their position as the largest Airbnb markets in this dataset. Paris skews heavily toward entire-home listings (88.2%), while London has a more balanced mix with 34.9% private rooms.</div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2 -->
<div class="section" id="pricing-analysis">
    <h2><span class="section-num">2</span>Pricing Dynamics Across Cities</h2>
    <p class="section-objective">Compare median and average nightly prices by city and room type, identify the most and least expensive markets, and highlight price dispersion within each city.</p>
    <div class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-value">$1,400</div><div class="kpi-label">Highest Median Price (Bangkok)</div></div>
        <div class="kpi-card alt"><div class="kpi-value">$131</div><div class="kpi-label">Lowest Median Price (Rome)</div></div>
        <div class="kpi-card accent"><div class="kpi-value">$222</div><div class="kpi-label">Amsterdam Median</div></div>
        <div class="kpi-card"><div class="kpi-value">2.55</div><div class="kpi-label">Highest Price CV (London)</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="highlight-box"><strong>Pricing Note:</strong> Bangkok's median price of $1,400 likely reflects incomplete USD normalization from Thai Baht. Excluding Bangkok, Amsterdam ($222) commands the highest median nightly rate, while Rome ($131) and Barcelona ($132) offer the most affordable markets. Paris and Sydney are absent due to missing price data.</div>
    <div class="chart-container"><canvas id="chartMedianPrice"></canvas></div>
    <h3 class="section-sub">Median Price by City and Room Type</h3>
    <div class="chart-container"><canvas id="chartPriceByRoom"></canvas></div>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>City</th><th>Entire Home/Apt</th><th>Private Room</th><th>Shared Room</th><th>Hotel Room</th></tr></thead>
